win32u: Ignore Alt's key repeats when deciding whether Alt was pressed alone.

GitHub Neutron#35 (Premiere Pro): "on Premiere it doesn't get triggered when you hold Alt to zoom with the scroll
wheel. However it does happen if you hold it for a short moment, even if you scrolled."

DefWindowProc toggled menu_sys_key ("Alt pressed alone") on every WM_SYSKEYDOWN of Alt, the key repeats of a held
Alt included, so whether its release opened the menu bar depended on how many repeats came before it: opened after
0, 2 or 8 repeats, not after 1 or 3. A repeat (KEYDATA_PREVSTATE) is not a new press; it now leaves the state as it
is. ReactOS skips repeats here too. Alt+F4 still acts on repeats.

Measured on Windows 11 build 26200 with harnesses/alt-repeat-menu.c, through DefWindowProc directly and through
SendInput: Alt released after 0, 1, 2, 3 or 8 repeats opens the menu once every time, with nothing else pressed,
after a wheel notch or after a mouse move; a click cancels it. Wine with this patch gives the same table.

Alone, this makes a held Alt+wheel in Premiere open the menu every time (it was shut by the toggling); the next
patch (the menu does not start while a window holds the capture) is what keeps it shut, as on Windows. Gate:
NEUTRON_ALT_REPEAT=0 restores the toggling.

--- a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
@@ -40,6 +40,14 @@
 static short f10_key = 0;
 static short menu_sys_key = 0;
 
+/* NEUTRON alt-repeat: see WM_SYSKEYDOWN */
+static BOOL neutron_alt_repeat(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) { const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_ALT_REPEAT" ); on = !(e && e[0] == '0'); }
+    return on;
+}
+
 static BOOL has_dialog_frame( UINT style, UINT ex_style )
 {
     return (ex_style & WS_EX_DLGMODALFRAME) || ((style & WS_DLGFRAME) && !(style & WS_THICKFRAME));
@@ -2859,10 +2867,19 @@
     case WM_SYSKEYDOWN:
         if (HIWORD( lparam ) & KEYDATA_ALT)
         {
-            if ((wparam == VK_MENU || wparam == VK_LMENU || wparam == VK_RMENU) && !menu_sys_key)
-                menu_sys_key = 1;
-            else
-                menu_sys_key = 0;
+            /* NEUTRON alt-repeat (GitHub Neutron#35): a key held down repeats; the repeats (KEYDATA_PREVSTATE) are not new
+             * presses and leave the "Alt pressed alone" state as it is. Toggling it on each of them made the menu depend
+             * on how many repeats came before the release. Measured on Windows 11 build 26200 (harnesses/alt-repeat-menu.exe,
+             * DefWindowProc and SendInput): Alt released after 0, 1, 2, 3 or 8 repeats opens the menu once every time; here
+             * it opened after 0, 2 and 8 and not after 1 or 3. ReactOS skips repeats here too. Alt+F4 below still acts on
+             * repeats. Kill switch NEUTRON_ALT_REPEAT=0. */
+            if (!(HIWORD( lparam ) & KEYDATA_PREVSTATE) || !neutron_alt_repeat())
+            {
+                if ((wparam == VK_MENU || wparam == VK_LMENU || wparam == VK_RMENU) && !menu_sys_key)
+                    menu_sys_key = 1;
+                else
+                    menu_sys_key = 0;
+            }
 
             f10_key = 0;
 
